-- title:
--   Density of Dyadic Rationals
-- statement:
--   The set `dyadicRationals = {k·2^{-n} : k ∈ ℤ, n ∈ ℕ}` is dense in ℝ. Equivalently, every real x and every radius r > 0 admit a dyadic rational within distance r of x. The lemma `dense_dyadicRationals` supplies the dense domain used in the deterministic Kolmogorov–Chentsov extension argument.
